in", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to achieve", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peru gained independence in 1921.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "independence", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the state of being self-governing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peru's independence began in 1921.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gift", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a present", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The museum was a gift from Italy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "contemporary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "modern", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are examples of contemporary art in the Italian Museum.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the Americas", "type": "name"}, {"content": "North America and South America", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is the oldest house in the Americas.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "guidebook ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a book with information about a place for tourists", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My guidebook has information about Algia House.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "GPS ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "global positioning system; a device that tells you where you are in the world", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have my GPS so I won't get lost.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le15ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Showing Interest", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "To show interest in what another person is saying, you can ask questions. This shows that you are listening and want to know more about what that person said. <br><br>You can ask both Yes/No questions and Wh- Hw questions.<br><br>  You can also make comments such as: <span class = \"italic\"> Very interesting</span> or  <span class = \"italic\">How fascinating</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: On the right, you can see the Italian Museum.<br><span class=\"strong\">Tourist</span>: Italian? Aren't we in Peru?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: The Italians gave the museum as a gift. <br><span class=\"strong\">Tourist</span>: Very interesting.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Prepare for a trip to Peru, and make a list of ten things you want to pack in your suitcase.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Have your partner do the same, and share your list with your partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about the differences and/or similarities between your lists.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about necessary things to take on a trip.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make a packing list of ten things.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss my list with my partner and make comparisons.", "type": "text"}]}]}